+## ADR-396 - The Trace dialog says what the tracer uses (2026-09-25)
+
+**Status:** Accepted. | **Date:** 2026-09-25
+
+### Context
+
+The 2026-09-24 tracer audit compared the Trace Image dialog's controls, notes and previews with what
+the engine does. In the dialog it found:
+
+- Edge Detection results engrave as lines: a Line operation for vectors and Outlines for raster
+  scan (ADR-235, decision 2). The preview, Overlay and Multi-File Trace SVGs filled them, so the
+  operator saw solid letters that would burn only as outlines.
+- Switching Smooth, Sharp or Centerline from automatic detection to Manual brightness band started
+  the band at 0–128. The automatic (Otsu) threshold can be far from 128: in the audit's example,
+  light ink at brightness 150 got a threshold of 197, and the 0–128 band then traced nothing. The
+  tracing lesson tells operators to make exactly this switch.
+- Line Art's automatic detection is a fixed 0–128 band, plus marks darker than their surroundings
+  only when a colour check passes (`auto-sketch-trace.ts`). The dialog showed neither the band nor
+  which route ran, and its label and description promised pale details on every image.
+- Large images are traced on a decoded grid of at most 2048 px a side. Remove ink specks, Ignore
+  Less Than, Minimum line and Centerline's join gap count pixels of that grid, but the dialog showed
+  only the image's own size.
+- Hints disagreed with the engine. Edge Detail claimed to smooth noise; the detector reads it only as
+  the neighbourhood size (`edge-input.ts`, about 25 px at 0 to 6 px at 100). Sensitivity and Detail
+  also rewrote the high ratio and join gap, which nothing reads. Area fields accepted fractions the
+  tracer rounds.
+- Adjustments carry over between styles, but "Settings edited" appeared for kept values the
+  selected style ignores, and selecting Photo shading overwrote an Enhance region choice for good.
+- Centerline joins facing line ends closer than `centerlineJoinGapPx` (3 px in its preset,
+  `junction-pairing.ts`) with no control for it.
+- Smooth and Sharp promised curve styles that on anti-aliased art they did not deliver (audit
+  finding 9). They differ from Line Art in detection and cleanup.
+- LightBurn opens Trace Image with Alt/Option+T
+  (https://docs.lightburnsoftware.com/2.1/Reference/TraceImage/). KerfDesk had no shortcut.
+
+### Decision
+
+1. **A trace reports what it chose; nothing reads it back.** Trace steps may yield a display-only
+   report (`TraceReport` in `trace-steps.ts`): the luma the automatic threshold picked, and whether
+   Line Art added local-contrast marks. The worker, the inline fallback, region crop and enhance
+   and the preview carry it. The options that key prepared and cached results are unchanged, and so
+   is trace output. The dialog uses the latest finished preview's report only while the image,
+   region and detection options match what was traced; finishing controls (Smoothness, Optimize,
+   Ignore Less Than, Join gaps) keep it (`use-trace-preview-facts.ts`).
+2. **Manual starts where automatic was.** Otsu inks luma below its threshold T, and the manual band
+   is inclusive, so the first switch to Manual on an automatic-threshold preset sets Threshold to
+   T − 1: the same pixels stay ink. A band the operator already set is kept. Without a matching
+   report the band still starts at 0–128.
+3. **Automatic shows its band.** In automatic and Faint lines modes the Detection section shows the
+   band in use, read-only, and Line Art says which route ran. Line Art's Detection label reads
+   "Automatic (band + pale colour detail)".
+4. **Pixel settings name their grid.** When the traced grid differs from the image, the settings
+   panel says "Tracing at W × H px; pixel settings use this grid."
+5. **Hints come from the engine.** Each numeric control has a unit and a hint checked against the
+   code; area fields step and round to whole pixels; a Cutoff above Threshold says which pixels the
+   band selects, since the engine orders the two ends. Edge Sensitivity is shown from, and writes,
+   only the low ratio the detector reads; Detail writes only the blur sigma. The Smoothness hint
+   uses potrace's corner semantics (https://potrace.sourceforge.net/potrace.1.html: alphamax 0
+   gives a polygon, above 4/3 no corners), matching LightBurn's 0 = lines, 1.33 = curves.
+6. **Edge Detection previews as strokes.** The preview, Overlay and Multi-File Trace SVGs draw Edge
+   results as lines, like Centerline, with one-screen-pixel preview strokes at any zoom. This
+   applies ADR-235's output semantics to the preview; the committed output is unchanged.
+7. **Kept adjustments are named.** "Settings edited" counts only adjustments the selected style
+   uses and that change its options. The preset hint names kept adjustments the style ignores
+   ("Not used by Line Art: Sensitivity."). Photo shading forces Crop while selected but keeps the
+   operator's boundary mode for the other styles.
+8. **Centerline gets Join gaps** (0–50 px; the preset's 3 by default). It maps to
+   `centerlineJoinGapPx`; 0 turns the end bridge off. It applies only to Centerline.
+9. **Smooth and Sharp describe what differs.** Smooth sets its threshold from the image and removes
+   isolated noise dots when there are many. Sharp sets its threshold from the image, keeps
+   single-pixel marks and tiny holes, and rounds fewer corners into curves.
+10. **Alt+T (Option+T on macOS) opens Trace Image** for the selected image with the Trace command's
+    gate, and not while a dialog, the canvas text editor or a text field owns the keyboard. Because
+    macOS Option composes a character (Option+T types "†"), Alt chords match the physical key when
+    no plain letter was typed; Alt+M gets the same fix. The command, Keyboard Shortcuts list and
+    tracing lesson show the chord.
+11. **Multi-File Trace keeps one Save dialog per SVG.** A one-folder export is left for a later
+    decision; see Consequences.
+
+### Consequences
+
+- A trace yields its report once. Runners that do not show reports treat it as one more
+  checkpoint.
+- The report is only as fresh as the last finished preview. Until the preview finishes, Automatic
+  says the band will be set from the image, and Manual starts at 0–128.
+- Some texts rely on engine changes made alongside this decision in the same audit batch: the
+  Smoothness and Optimize hints and Sharp's corner claim on Smoothness acting on every image with
+  potrace semantics; the speck hint on corner-touching pixels counting as one mark; and the Minimum
+  line hint on holes being kept. If one of those changes is withdrawn, its text must change too.
+- Pixel values still mean grid pixels, not source pixels; the note makes the grid visible rather
+  than converting settings between grids.
+- The Alt chords follow the typed letter when a letter is typed, so on Dvorak Alt+T is the key
+  labelled T. Where Option types a symbol, the physical key decides, so a Dvorak Mac user presses
+  Option on the key in the QWERTY T position. The chords were checked with synthetic key events,
+  not on real keyboards. The desktop menu policy defines no item of its own on Alt/Option+T
+  (`electron/application-menu-policy.ts`).
+- Multi-File Trace to one folder is not done, because it is not a desktop-only change and needs
+  its own design. The desktop app uses the web adapter (`src/ui/app/main.tsx`), so the folder flow
+  would change the web build too. Tiled G-code export reserves its folder before any work because
+  web pickers consume the click's user activation (`save-tiled-gcode.ts`); Multi-File Trace spends
+  that activation on the file-open picker, so a folder needs a second click. A write into a
+  reserved folder replaces a file with the same name (`web-adapter.ts`), so a batch export also
+  needs a collision policy.
